/-!
# Exactness of the sequence of sheaves of units of a squishing

Let `k` be an algebraically closed field and let `f : X' ⟶ X` be the squishing of a tangent
vector `ϑ` of an algebraic `k`-scheme `X'`, in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 0C1K]. The exact
sequence of Picard groups of [Stacks, Tag 0C1N] is read off the short exact sequence of
sheaves of *units* on `X`

`1 ⟶ 𝒪_X^* ⟶ f_*𝒪_{X'}^* ⟶ (k, +)_x ⟶ 1`,

whose quotient map is the logarithmic `ε`-derivative along `ϑ`. That quotient map is
`Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.epsilonLogDerivSheafHom`; what is proved here is that the
sequence it sits in is short exact. The connecting homomorphism of that sequence is then the
tangent homomorphism `(k, +) ⟶ Pic(X)` which is the first map of the sequence of Tag 0C1N, and
it is constructed here too, together with the description of its kernel and its injectivity on
a proper reduced `X'`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.picardTangentHom` — **the tangent homomorphism**
  `(k, +) ⟶ Pic(X)`.
* `Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.unitsComplex` and
  `Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.connectingHom` — the short exact sequence of sheaves of units and
  its connecting map.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.shortExact_units_of_isSquishingTangentVector` — **the short exact
  sequence of sheaves of units of a squishing**, for the named maps
  `Stacks.GlueSquishUnits.unitsPushforwardMap` (pullback of units along `f`) and
  `Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.epsilonLogDerivSheafHom`, both of which are pinned down on
  sections.
* `Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.exists_globalUnit_epsilonLogDeriv_eq_of_picardTangentHom_eq_zero` —
  a scalar killed by the tangent homomorphism is the logarithmic `ε`-derivative of a unit on the
  whole of `X'`; equivalently, the kernel of the tangent homomorphism is the image of
  `𝒪^*(X') → (k, +)`.
* `Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.injective_picardTangentHom_of_isProper_of_isReduced` — **the
  tangent homomorphism is injective** when `X'` is proper over `k` and reduced.

## Implementation notes

Surjectivity of the quotient map reduces to one statement about the stalk `B` of `f_*𝒪_{X'}` at
the contracted point: that the restriction `B ⟶ k[ε]` along `ϑ`, the inclusion `A = 𝒪_{X, x} ⟶ B`
and the `ε`-coefficient `B ⟶ k` form a *coefficient sequence*, meaning that the `ε`-coefficient
is surjective with kernel the image of `A`, that the constant coefficient `A ⟶ k` is surjective,
and that the two agree on the image of `A` in the evident way. Such a sequence makes `B` a
finite `A`-module — it is generated by `1` and any lift of `ε` — hence `A ⟶ B` integral, hence
the kernel of `B ⟶ k[ε]` contained in the Jacobson radical of `B`, hence `Bˣ ⟶ k[ε]^*`
surjective, which gives the surjectivity of the logarithmic derivative on units. This is
`dlog_units_surjective_of_coefficient_sequence`, and the hypotheses of a coefficient sequence
are exactly what the short exact sequence of additive sheaves of Tag 0C1K provides at the
contracted point.

Injectivity of the first map and exactness in the middle need no locality: a unit of
`Γ(X', f⁻¹U)` killed by the logarithmic derivative has, together with its inverse, a preimage
under `f.app U` by exactness of the additive sequence *on sections over `U`*, and those two
preimages are mutually inverse because `f.app U` is injective. The sectionwise statement is
`TopCat.Sheaf.sections_exact_of_left_exact`, available because the forgetful functor to
presheaves is left exact.

The contracted point is named `Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.squishedPoint` rather than written out
as `(ϑ ≫ f).base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint k[ε])`. The reason is that
`IsLocalRing.closedPoint k[ε]` is an element of `PrimeSpectrum k[ε]` rather than of the carrier
of the scheme `Spec k[ε]`, and the two agree only after unfolding `AlgebraicGeometry.Spec`; a
goal mentioning that spelling is not type-correct at the transparency level `rw` and `simp`
work at, so neither tactic will act on it. A definition whose *declared* type is already the
carrier of `X` has no such defect, and the membership hypotheses are converted between the
three spellings the consumers want by `mem_comp` and `mem_preimage`. For the same reason the
proofs below use `Eq.trans` and `congrArg` where `rw` would be shorter.

Sections of the additive skyscraper over a neighbourhood of its point are the ground field only
after rewriting the defining `if`. The identification is `skyscraperAddSheafVal`, built on
`Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.skyscraperAddSheaf_obj_eq`, and its properties — that it
undoes `Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.skyscraperAddSheafMk`, that it is compatible with
restriction, and that it is injective — are what the quotient maps are read through. The
compatibility with restriction is obtained from
`StalkSkyscraperPresheafAdjunctionAuxs.germ_fromStalk`, which is the one
statement relating sections of a skyscraper to its stalk without touching the `if`.

The tangent homomorphism is built exactly as its glueing counterpart
`Stacks.GluePicard.picardGluingHom` is: the low-degree cohomology sequence
`Stacks.Cohomology.AbelianColimit.H'longExactSequence_exact` over the open `⊤` in degrees `0`
and `1`, the identification of degree-zero native cohomology with sections
(`Stacks.GluePicard.h0Iso`) and of degree-one native cohomology of the units sheaf with the
Picard group (`Stacks.GluePicard.h1UnitsAddEquivOfScheme`). Unlike the glueing case the two maps
of the sequence here are *named* rather than produced existentially, so no structure bundling a
chosen sequence is needed; `unitsComplex` is the short complex of those two maps.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C1K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C1K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C1N](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C1N)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C1M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C1M)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.SquishSheafSequence
open Stacks.GlueSquishUnits (ringPushforwardMap skyscraperPresheaf_obj_eq
  skyscraperPresheaf_map_comp unitsPushforwardMap unitsPushforwardMap_app)

open Stacks.Cohomology.Generators (unitsSheaf)

/-! ### The contracted point -/

/-- **The point of `X` to which `f` contracts the tangent vector `θ`.**

It is given a name of its own because `AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector` spells it
`(θ ≫ f).base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))`, and the closed point of
`Spec k[ε]` is an element of `PrimeSpectrum k[ε]` rather than of the carrier of the scheme
`Spec k[ε]`: the two agree only after unfolding `AlgebraicGeometry.Spec`, so a goal mentioning
that spelling is not type-correct at the transparency level `rw` works at and `rw` refuses to
act on it. A definition whose *declared* type is already the carrier of `X` has no such
defect. -/
def squishedPoint {k : Type u} [Field k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X)
    (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X') : X :=
  (θ ≫ f).base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))

/-- `Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.squishedPoint` is the image of the closed point of
`Spec k[ε]`. -/
theorem squishedPoint_eq {k : Type u} [Field k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X)
    (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X') :
    squishedPoint f θ = (θ ≫ f).base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k)) := rfl

/-- The spelling of membership that the clauses of
`AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector` consume. -/
private theorem mem_comp {k : Type u} [Field k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X)
    (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X') {U : X.Opens} (hz : squishedPoint f θ ∈ U) :
    (θ ≫ f).base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k)) ∈ U := hz

/-- The closed point of the tangent vector lies in the preimage of `U` exactly when the
contracted point lies in `U`; this is the spelling the maps upstairs want. -/
theorem mem_preimage {k : Type u} [Field k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X)
    (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X') {U : X.Opens} (hz : squishedPoint f θ ∈ U) :
    θ.base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k)) ∈ f ⁻¹ᵁ U := hz

/-! ### Sections of a skyscraper sheaf -/

/-- **A section of the additive skyscraper at `x` over an open containing `x`, read as a scalar.**
It is through this reading, rather than through a transported equality, that the quotient maps of
the two sequences are pinned down on sections. -/
def skyscraperAddSheafVal {k : Type u} [Field k] (X : Scheme.{u}) (x : X) {U : X.Opens}
    (hx : x ∈ U) (s : (skyscraperAddSheaf (k := k) X x).obj.obj (op U)) : k :=
  (eqToHom (skyscraperAddSheaf_obj_eq X x hx)) s

/-- `Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.skyscraperAddSheafVal` undoes the reading of a scalar as a
section of the additive skyscraper. -/
theorem skyscraperAddSheafVal_mk {k : Type u} [Field k] (X : Scheme.{u}) (x : X)
    {U : X.Opens} (hx : x ∈ U) (c : k) :
    skyscraperAddSheafVal X x hx (skyscraperAddSheafMk X x hx c) = c :=
  eqToHom_skyscraperAddSheafMk X x hx c

/-- `Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.skyscraperAddSheafVal` is injective, being an isomorphism. -/
private theorem skyscraperAddSheafVal_injective {k : Type u} [Field k] (X : Scheme.{u}) (x : X)
    {U : X.Opens} (hx : x ∈ U) :
    Function.Injective (skyscraperAddSheafVal (k := k) X x hx) :=
  (ConcreteCategory.bijective_of_isIso
    (eqToHom (skyscraperAddSheaf_obj_eq (k := k) X x hx))).1

/-- `Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.skyscraperAddSheafVal` sends the zero section to zero. -/
private theorem skyscraperAddSheafVal_zero {k : Type u} [Field k] (X : Scheme.{u}) (x : X)
    {U : X.Opens} (hx : x ∈ U) : skyscraperAddSheafVal (k := k) X x hx 0 = 0 :=
  map_zero _

/-- A section of the additive skyscraper vanishes exactly when its scalar reading does. -/
private theorem skyscraperAddSheafVal_eq_zero_iff {k : Type u} [Field k] (X : Scheme.{u})
    (x : X) {U : X.Opens} (hx : x ∈ U) {s : (skyscraperAddSheaf (k := k) X x).obj.obj (op U)} :
    skyscraperAddSheafVal X x hx s = 0 ↔ s = 0 :=
  (skyscraperAddSheafVal_injective X x hx).eq_iff' (skyscraperAddSheafVal_zero X x hx)

/-- **Reading a section of the additive skyscraper as a scalar is unchanged by restriction** to
a smaller open still containing the point. -/
theorem skyscraperAddSheafVal_res {k : Type u} [Field k] (X : Scheme.{u}) (x : X)
    {U V : X.Opens} (i : V ⟶ U) (hx : x ∈ V)
    (s : (skyscraperAddSheaf (k := k) X x).obj.obj (op U)) :
    skyscraperAddSheafVal X x hx ((skyscraperAddSheaf (k := k) X x).obj.map i.op s) =
      skyscraperAddSheafVal X x (i.le hx) s := by
  classical
  exact congrArg (fun g : AddCommGrpCat.Hom _ _ => g.hom s)
    (skyscraperPresheaf_map_comp x (AddCommGrpCat.of k) i hx)

/-! ### Exactness of a sequence of sheaves of abelian groups from its sections -/

/-- A sequence of sheaves of abelian groups is exact once, over every open, a section of the
middle sheaf killed by the second map is in the image of the first. -/
private theorem exact_of_sections {T : TopCat.{u}}
    (S : ShortComplex (TopCat.Sheaf AddCommGrpCat.{u} T))
    (hS : ∀ (U : Opens T) (b : S.X₂.obj.obj (op U)), S.g.hom.app (op U) b = 0 →
      ∃ a, S.f.hom.app (op U) a = b) : S.Exact := by
  rw [TopCat.Sheaf.exact_iff_stalkFunctor_map_exact]
  intro x
  rw [ShortComplex.ab_exact_iff]
  intro b hb
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, s, rfl⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq S.X₂.obj b
  change (TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor AddCommGrpCat x).map S.g.hom
    (S.X₂.presheaf.germ U x hxU s) = 0 at hb
  rw [TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor_map_germ_apply] at hb
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, i, j, hij⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.germ_eq S.X₃.obj x hxU hxU
    (S.g.hom.app (op U) s) 0 (by rw [map_zero]; exact hb)
  have hs : S.g.hom.app (op V) (S.X₂.obj.map i.op s) = 0 := by
    rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, S.g.hom.naturality]
    simpa using hij
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hS V _ hs
  refine ⟨S.X₁.presheaf.germ V x hxV a, ?_⟩
  show (TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor AddCommGrpCat x).map S.f.hom _ = _
  rw [TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor_map_germ_apply, ha, TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply]

/-! ### The sequence of additive sheaves, with the contracted point named -/

/-- The short exact sequence of additive sheaves of [Stacks, Tag 0C1K], with the contracted
point spelled `Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.squishedPoint`. -/
private theorem shortExact_addSheaf {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    {X' X : Scheme.{u}} [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ) :
    ∃ (ψ : pushforwardAddSheaf f ⟶ skyscraperAddSheaf (k := k) X (squishedPoint f θ))
      (hzero : structureToPushforwardAddSheaf f ≫ ψ = 0),
      (ShortComplex.mk (structureToPushforwardAddSheaf f) ψ hzero).ShortExact ∧
        ∀ (U : X.Opens) (hz : squishedPoint f θ ∈ U) (s : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U)),
          ψ.hom.app (op U) s =
            skyscraperAddSheafMk X (squishedPoint f θ) hz
              (epsilonCoefficientAt θ (f ⁻¹ᵁ U) (mem_preimage f θ hz) s) :=
  shortExact_of_isSquishingTangentVector f θ h

/-! ### The logarithmic derivative on the dual numbers -/

/-- The logarithmic `ε`-derivative of a unit of the dual numbers, as a homomorphism from the
additively written group of units to the additive group of the ground field. -/
private def dualNumberDlogHom {k : Type u} [Field k] : Additive ((DualNumber k)ˣ) →+ k where
  toFun a := (a.toMul : DualNumber k).snd / (a.toMul : DualNumber k).fst
  map_zero' := by simp
  map_add' a b := by
    have ha : (a.toMul : DualNumber k).fst ≠ 0 :=
      (TrivSqZeroExt.isUnit_iff_isUnit_fst.mp a.toMul.isUnit).ne_zero
    have hb : (b.toMul : DualNumber k).fst ≠ 0 :=
      (TrivSqZeroExt.isUnit_iff_isUnit_fst.mp b.toMul.isUnit).ne_zero
    change ((a.toMul * b.toMul : (DualNumber k)ˣ) : DualNumber k).snd /
      ((a.toMul * b.toMul : (DualNumber k)ˣ) : DualNumber k).fst = _
    rw [Units.val_mul, TrivSqZeroExt.fst_mul, TrivSqZeroExt.snd_mul, op_smul_eq_mul,
      smul_eq_mul]
    field_simp
    ring

/-- **The logarithmic `ε`-derivative is surjective on the units of the dual numbers**: the unit
`1 + cε` has logarithmic derivative `c`. -/
private theorem dualNumberDlogHom_surjective {k : Type u} [Field k] :
    Function.Surjective (dualNumberDlogHom (k := k)) := by
  intro c
  have hd : IsUnit (1 + TrivSqZeroExt.inr c : DualNumber k) :=
    TrivSqZeroExt.isUnit_iff_isUnit_fst.2 (by simp)
  refine ⟨Additive.ofMul hd.unit, ?_⟩
  show (hd.unit : DualNumber k).snd / (hd.unit : DualNumber k).fst = c
  rw [hd.unit_spec]
  simp

/-! ### Coefficient sequences -/

/-- **A surjection whose kernel is contained in the Jacobson radical is surjective on units.**
A preimage of a unit has a product with a preimage of its inverse which differs from `1` by an
element of the Jacobson radical, hence is a unit, hence so is the preimage itself. -/
private theorem units_map_surjective_of_ker_le_jacobson {R S : Type u} [CommRing R] [CommRing S]
    (q : R →+* S) (hq : Function.Surjective q) (hker : RingHom.ker q ≤ Ring.jacobson R) :
    Function.Surjective (Units.map q.toMonoidHom : Rˣ → Sˣ) := by
  intro u
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := hq (u : S)
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := hq ((u⁻¹ : Sˣ) : S)
  have hxy : x * y - 1 ∈ Ring.jacobson R := hker (by
    show q (x * y - 1) = 0
    rw [map_sub, map_mul, hx, hy]
    simp)
  have hxyUnit : IsUnit (x * y) :=
    Ideal.isUnit_of_sub_one_mem_jacobson_bot (x * y) (by
      simpa only [← Ideal.jacobson_bot] using hxy)
  exact ⟨(IsUnit.mul_iff.mp hxyUnit).1.unit, Units.ext hx⟩

/-- **The image of the maximal ideal of a local ring under an integral ring homomorphism lies in
the Jacobson radical.** Every maximal ideal upstairs contracts to a maximal ideal downstairs,
which is *the* maximal ideal. -/
private theorem map_maximalIdeal_le_jacobson_of_integral {A B : Type u} [CommRing A]
    [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing A] (i : A →+* B) (hi : i.IsIntegral) :
    Ideal.map i (IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A) ≤ Ring.jacobson B := by
  rw [Ring.jacobson_eq_sInf_isMaximal]
  refine Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.mpr fun b hb => ?_
  show i b ∈ sInf {M : Ideal B | M.IsMaximal}
  rw [Ideal.mem_sInf]
  intro M hM
  have hM' : M.IsMaximal := hM
  have hcomap : M.comap i = IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A :=
    IsLocalRing.eq_maximalIdeal (Ideal.isMaximal_comap_of_isIntegral_of_isMaximal' i hi M)
  show b ∈ M.comap i
  rw [hcomap]
  exact hb

/-- **The restriction map of a coefficient sequence is surjective.** A dual number is the sum of
a constant lifted from `A` and a lift of its `ε`-coefficient corrected by a constant. -/
private theorem coefficient_sequence_surjective {A B k : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [CommRing k] (i : A →+* B) (q : B →+* DualNumber k) (r : A →+* k) (d : B →+ k)
    (hfst : ∀ a, (q (i a)).fst = r a) (hsnd : ∀ a, (q (i a)).snd = 0)
    (hcoeff : ∀ b, (q b).snd = d b) (hd : Function.Surjective d)
    (hrange : Function.Surjective r) : Function.Surjective q := by
  intro z
  obtain ⟨a₀, ha₀⟩ := hrange z.fst
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hd z.snd
  obtain ⟨a₁, ha₁⟩ := hrange (q b).fst
  refine ⟨i a₀ + (b - i a₁), TrivSqZeroExt.ext ?_ ?_⟩
  all_goals simp [map_add, map_sub, hfst, ha₀, ha₁, hsnd, hcoeff, hb]

/-- **A coefficient sequence makes `B` a finite `A`-module**, generated by `1` and any element
whose restriction is `ε`. -/
private theorem finite_of_coefficient_sequence {A B k : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B]
    [CommRing k] (i : A →+* B) (q : B →+* DualNumber k) (r : A →+* k) (d : B →+ k)
    (hfst : ∀ a, (q (i a)).fst = r a) (hsnd : ∀ a, (q (i a)).snd = 0)
    (hcoeff : ∀ b, (q b).snd = d b) (hker : ∀ b, d b = 0 → ∃ a, i a = b)
    (hd : Function.Surjective d) (hrange : Function.Surjective r) : i.Finite := by
  classical
  let : Algebra A B := i.toAlgebra
  obtain ⟨e, he⟩ :=
    coefficient_sequence_surjective i q r d hfst hsnd hcoeff hd hrange (TrivSqZeroExt.inr 1)
  have hefst : (q e).fst = 0 := by rw [he]; simp
  have hesnd : (q e).snd = 1 := by rw [he]; simp
  have hspan : Submodule.span A (↑({1, e} : Finset B) : Set B) = ⊤ := by
    refine top_unique fun b _ => ?_
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hrange (q b).fst
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := hrange (q b).snd
    have hqdiff : q (b - i a - i c * e) = 0 := by
      refine TrivSqZeroExt.ext ?_ ?_
      · simp [map_sub, map_mul, hfst, ha, hc, hefst]
      · simp [map_sub, map_mul, hsnd, hfst, hc, hefst, hesnd]
    obtain ⟨a₀, ha₀⟩ := hker _ (by rw [← hcoeff]; exact congrArg TrivSqZeroExt.snd hqdiff)
    have hbform : b = i a₀ + i a + i c * e := by
      calc
        b = (b - i a - i c * e) + i a + i c * e := by ring
        _ = i a₀ + i a + i c * e := by rw [ha₀]
    rw [hbform]
    have h1 : i a₀ + i a = (a₀ + a) • (1 : B) := by
      rw [← map_add]
      simp [Algebra.smul_def, RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra i]
    have h2 : i c * e = c • e := by
      simp [Algebra.smul_def, RingHom.algebraMap_toAlgebra i]
    rw [h1, h2]
    exact add_mem (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span (by simp)))
      (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ (Submodule.subset_span (by simp)))
  show Module.Finite A B
  exact Module.Finite.of_fg_top ⟨{1, e}, hspan⟩

/-- **The logarithmic `ε`-derivative on units is surjective for a coefficient sequence.** The
sequence makes `A ⟶ B` integral, so the kernel of `B ⟶ k[ε]` — which is the image of the
maximal ideal of `A` — lies in the Jacobson radical of `B`; the restriction is therefore
surjective on units, and the logarithmic derivative is already surjective on the units of
`k[ε]`. -/
private theorem dlog_units_surjective_of_coefficient_sequence {A B k : Type u} [CommRing A]
    [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing A] [Field k] (i : A →+* B) (q : B →+* DualNumber k) (r : A →+* k)
    (d : B →+ k) (hfst : ∀ a, (q (i a)).fst = r a) (hsnd : ∀ a, (q (i a)).snd = 0)
    (hcoeff : ∀ b, (q b).snd = d b) (hker : ∀ b, d b = 0 → ∃ a, i a = b)
    (hd : Function.Surjective d) (hrange : Function.Surjective r)
    (himage : ∀ a, a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A → i a ∈ Ring.jacobson B) :
    Function.Surjective
      (fun b : Bˣ => dualNumberDlogHom (Additive.ofMul (Units.map q.toMonoidHom b))) := by
  have hres : ∀ a, r a = 0 → a ∈ IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A := by
    intro a ha
    rw [IsLocalRing.mem_maximalIdeal]
    intro hua
    have hru : IsUnit (r a) := hua.map r
    rw [ha] at hru
    simp at hru
  have hjac : RingHom.ker q ≤ Ring.jacobson B := by
    intro b hb
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hker b (by rw [← hcoeff, hb]; rfl)
    have hqa : q (i a) = 0 := by rw [ha, hb]
    have hra : r a = 0 := by rw [← hfst a, hqa]; rfl
    rw [← ha]
    exact himage a (hres a hra)
  have hq := coefficient_sequence_surjective i q r d hfst hsnd hcoeff hd hrange
  refine dualNumberDlogHom_surjective.comp fun a => ?_
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := units_map_surjective_of_ker_le_jacobson q hq hjac a.toMul
  exact ⟨b, by simpa [hb]⟩

/-! ### Two auxiliary surjectivity statements -/

/-- **A tangent vector defined over `k` restricts the constant global sections to the constant
dual numbers.** This is where the hypothesis that the vector is defined over `k` enters. -/
private theorem germ_stalkClosedPointTo_const {k : Type u} [Field k] {Y : Scheme.{u}}
    [Y.Over (Spec (.of k))] (η : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ Y)
    (hη : η ≫ (Y ↘ Spec (.of k)) = dualNumberToBase k) (c : k) :
    (Y.presheaf.germ ⊤ (η.base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) trivial ≫
          Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo η).hom
        (((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ (Y ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop).hom c) =
      algebraMap k (DualNumber k) c := by
  have hη' : η ≫ (Y ↘ Spec (.of k)) =
      Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k (DualNumber k))) := hη
  have hgerm : (Y ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫
      Y.presheaf.germ ⊤ (η.base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) trivial =
      (Spec (.of k)).presheaf.germ ⊤
          ((η ≫ (Y ↘ Spec (.of k))).base
            (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) trivial ≫
        (Y ↘ Spec (.of k)).stalkMap
          (η.base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) :=
    (Scheme.Hom.germ_stalkMap (Y ↘ Spec (.of k)) ⊤
      (η.base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) trivial).symm
  have step : (Y ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫
      Y.presheaf.germ ⊤ (η.base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) trivial ≫
        Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo η =
      (Spec (.of k)).presheaf.germ ⊤
          ((η ≫ (Y ↘ Spec (.of k))).base
            (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) trivial ≫
        Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo (η ≫ (Y ↘ Spec (.of k))) :=
    (Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
      (((congrArg (· ≫ Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo η) hgerm).trans
        (Category.assoc _ _ _)).trans
        (congrArg (fun m => (Spec (.of k)).presheaf.germ ⊤
            ((η ≫ (Y ↘ Spec (.of k))).base
              (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) trivial ≫ m)
          (Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo_comp η (Y ↘ Spec (.of k))).symm))
  have key : (Spec (.of k)).presheaf.germ ⊤
        ((η ≫ (Y ↘ Spec (.of k))).base
          (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) trivial ≫
      Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo (η ≫ (Y ↘ Spec (.of k))) =
      (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).hom ≫
        CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k (DualNumber k)) := by
    rw [hη']
    exact Scheme.germ_stalkClosedPointTo_Spec _
  have main : (Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ (Y ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫
      Y.presheaf.germ ⊤ (η.base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) trivial ≫
        Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo η =
      CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap k (DualNumber k)) := by
    rw [step, key, ← Category.assoc, Iso.inv_hom_id, Category.id_comp]
  show ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ (Y ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop ≫
    Y.presheaf.germ ⊤ (η.base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) trivial ≫
      Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo η).hom c = _
  rw [main]
  rfl

/-- **A tangent vector defined over `k` restricts the constant global sections to the constant
dual numbers.**

This is the form other modules use:
`Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.germ_stalkClosedPointTo_const` is private to this file. -/
alias germ_stalkClosedPointTo_const' := germ_stalkClosedPointTo_const

/-- **The constant coefficient of the restriction along a dual-number-valued point defined over
`k` is surjective on the stalk.** The germ of a constant global function is a preimage of that
constant. -/
private theorem constantCoefficient_surjective {k : Type u} [Field k] {Y : Scheme.{u}}
    [Y.Over (Spec (.of k))] (η : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ Y)
    (hη : η ≫ (Y ↘ Spec (.of k)) = dualNumberToBase k) :
    Function.Surjective (fun a => ((Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo η).hom a).fst) := by
  intro c
  refine ⟨Y.presheaf.germ ⊤ (η.base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) trivial
    (((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ (Y ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop).hom c), ?_⟩
  show ((Y.presheaf.germ ⊤ (η.base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) trivial ≫
      Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo η).hom
      (((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of k)).inv ≫ (Y ↘ Spec (.of k)).appTop).hom c)).fst = c
  rw [germ_stalkClosedPointTo_const η hη c, TrivSqZeroExt.algebraMap_eq_inl,
    TrivSqZeroExt.fst_inl]

/-- **A unit of the stalk of a ringed space is the germ of a unit on a neighbourhood.** -/
private theorem exists_unit_germ (Y : RingedSpace.{u, u}) (x : Y)
    (b : (Y.presheaf.stalk x)ˣ) {U : Opens Y} (hx : x ∈ U) :
    ∃ V ≤ U, ∃ (hxV : x ∈ V) (s : (Y.presheaf.obj (op V))ˣ),
      Units.map (Y.presheaf.germ V x hxV).hom.toMonoidHom s = b := by
  obtain ⟨W, hWU, hxW, t, ht⟩ := Y.presheaf.exists_le_germ_eq (b : Y.presheaf.stalk x) hx
  obtain ⟨V, i, hxV, hv⟩ := Y.isUnit_res_of_isUnit_germ W t x hxW (by rw [ht]; exact b.isUnit)
  refine ⟨V, i.le.trans hWU, hxV, hv.unit, Units.ext ?_⟩
  show (Y.presheaf.germ V x hxV) (hv.unit : Y.presheaf.obj (op V)) = (b : Y.presheaf.stalk x)
  rw [hv.unit_spec, Y.presheaf.germ_res_apply, ht]

/-- **A unit whose value and whose inverse's value are both in the image of an injective monoid
homomorphism is itself in the image of the induced map on units.** -/
private theorem units_map_range_of_values {A B : Type u} [Monoid A] [Monoid B] (i : A →* B)
    (hi : Function.Injective i) (b : Bˣ) (hb : ∃ a, i a = (b : B))
    (hb' : ∃ a, i a = ((b⁻¹ : Bˣ) : B)) : ∃ a : Aˣ, Units.map i a = b := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hb
  obtain ⟨a', ha'⟩ := hb'
  refine ⟨⟨a, a', ?_, ?_⟩, Units.ext (by simpa using ha)⟩
  all_goals apply hi
  all_goals simp [map_mul, ha, ha']

/-! ### The stalk of the pushforward at the contracted point -/

/-- The pushforward of the structure sheaf of `X'` along `f`, as a ringed space on `X`. Its
stalk at the contracted point is the ring over which the surjectivity of the logarithmic
derivative is checked. -/
def pushforwardRingedSpace {X' X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) : RingedSpace.{u, u} where
  carrier := X
  presheaf := f.base _* X'.presheaf
  IsSheaf := ((TopCat.Sheaf.pushforward CommRingCat.{u} f.base).obj
    X'.toLocallyRingedSpace.toRingedSpace.sheaf).property

/-- The map `A ⟶ B` of the coefficient sequence: the stalk of the comorphism of `f` at the
contracted point. -/
private def stalkToPushforwardStalk {k : Type u} [Field k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X)
    (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X') :
    X.presheaf.stalk (squishedPoint f θ) →+*
      (pushforwardRingedSpace f).presheaf.stalk (squishedPoint f θ) :=
  ((TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor CommRingCat.{u} (squishedPoint f θ)).map f.c).hom

/-- The map `B ⟶ k[ε]` of the coefficient sequence: restriction along the tangent vector. -/
private def pushforwardStalkToDualNumber {k : Type u} [Field k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X') :
    (pushforwardRingedSpace f).presheaf.stalk (squishedPoint f θ) →+* DualNumber k :=
  (X'.presheaf.stalkPushforward CommRingCat.{u} f.base
      (θ.base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) ≫
    Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo θ).hom

/-- The map `A ⟶ k` of the coefficient sequence: the constant coefficient of the restriction
along the tangent vector. -/
private def stalkToBase {k : Type u} [Field k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X)
    (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X') : X.presheaf.stalk (squishedPoint f θ) →+* k :=
  (TrivSqZeroExt.fstHom k k k).toRingHom.comp (Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo (θ ≫ f)).hom

/-- The map `B ⟶ k` of the coefficient sequence: the `ε`-coefficient of the restriction along
the tangent vector. -/
private def pushforwardStalkCoefficient {k : Type u} [Field k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X') :
    (pushforwardRingedSpace f).presheaf.stalk (squishedPoint f θ) →+ k where
  toFun b := (pushforwardStalkToDualNumber f θ b).snd
  map_zero' := by simp
  map_add' a b := by simp

/-- The two maps out of `B` agree: the second is the `ε`-coefficient of the first. -/
private theorem pushforwardStalkCoefficient_eq {k : Type u} [Field k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (b : (pushforwardRingedSpace f).presheaf.stalk (squishedPoint f θ)) :
    (pushforwardStalkToDualNumber f θ b).snd = pushforwardStalkCoefficient f θ b := rfl

/-- Restriction along the tangent vector agrees, on the image of the stalk downstairs, with
restriction along the contracted tangent vector. -/
private theorem pushforwardStalkToDualNumber_stalkToPushforwardStalk {k : Type u} [Field k]
    {X' X : Scheme.{u}} (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (a : X.presheaf.stalk (squishedPoint f θ)) :
    pushforwardStalkToDualNumber f θ (stalkToPushforwardStalk f θ a) =
      (Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo (θ ≫ f)).hom a := by
  rw [Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo_comp]
  rfl

/-- The germ of the pushforward at the contracted point, followed by the comparison with the
stalk upstairs, is the germ upstairs. -/
private theorem germ_comp_stalkPushforward {k : Type u} [Field k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X') (U : X.Opens)
    (hz : squishedPoint f θ ∈ U) :
    (pushforwardRingedSpace f).presheaf.germ U (squishedPoint f θ) hz ≫
        X'.presheaf.stalkPushforward CommRingCat.{u} f.base
          (θ.base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) =
      X'.presheaf.germ (f ⁻¹ᵁ U) (θ.base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k)))
        (mem_preimage f θ hz) :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.stalkPushforward_germ CommRingCat.{u} f.base X'.presheaf U
    (θ.base (IsLocalRing.closedPoint (DualNumber k))) (mem_preimage f θ hz)

/-- Restriction along the tangent vector, read on the germ of a section of the pushforward. -/
private theorem pushforwardStalkToDualNumber_germ {k : Type u} [Field k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X') (U : X.Opens)
    (hz : squishedPoint f θ ∈ U) (s : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U)) :
    pushforwardStalkToDualNumber f θ
        ((pushforwardRingedSpace f).presheaf.germ U (squishedPoint f θ) hz s) =
      sectionsToDualNumber θ (f ⁻¹ᵁ U) (mem_preimage f θ hz) s :=
  congrArg (fun m : _ ⟶ CommRingCat.of (DualNumber k) => m.hom s)
    ((Category.assoc _ _ _).symm.trans
      (congrArg (· ≫ Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo θ) (germ_comp_stalkPushforward f θ U hz)))

/-- The germ of the pullback of a section is the image of its germ under the stalk map. -/
private theorem stalkToPushforwardStalk_germ {k : Type u} [Field k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X') (U : X.Opens)
    (hz : squishedPoint f θ ∈ U) (s : Γ(X, U)) :
    stalkToPushforwardStalk f θ (X.presheaf.germ U (squishedPoint f θ) hz s) =
      (pushforwardRingedSpace f).presheaf.germ U (squishedPoint f θ) hz ((f.app U).hom s) :=
  TopCat.Presheaf.stalkFunctor_map_germ_apply U (squishedPoint f θ) hz f.c s

/-- The logarithmic `ε`-derivative of the germ of a unit of the pushforward is the logarithmic
`ε`-derivative of that unit. -/
private theorem dualNumberDlogHom_germ {k : Type u} [Field k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X') (U : X.Opens)
    (hz : squishedPoint f θ ∈ U) (s : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U)ˣ) :
    dualNumberDlogHom (Additive.ofMul (Units.map
        (pushforwardStalkToDualNumber f θ).toMonoidHom (Units.map
          ((pushforwardRingedSpace f).presheaf.germ U (squishedPoint f θ)
            hz).hom.toMonoidHom s))) =
      epsilonLogDeriv θ (f ⁻¹ᵁ U) (mem_preimage f θ hz) s := by
  have hq := pushforwardStalkToDualNumber_germ f θ U hz (s : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U))
  show (pushforwardStalkToDualNumber f θ
        ((pushforwardRingedSpace f).presheaf.germ U (squishedPoint f θ) hz
          (s : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U)))).snd /
      (pushforwardStalkToDualNumber f θ
        ((pushforwardRingedSpace f).presheaf.germ U (squishedPoint f θ) hz
          (s : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ U)))).fst = _
  rw [hq]
  rfl

/-! ### The short exact sequence of sheaves of units -/

/-- **The quotient map of the units sequence, read as a scalar, is the logarithmic
`ε`-derivative.** -/
theorem epsilonLogDerivSheafHom_val {k : Type u} [Field k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X') (V : X.Opens)
    (hz : squishedPoint f θ ∈ V) (s : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ V)ˣ) :
    skyscraperAddSheafVal (k := k) X (squishedPoint f θ) hz
        ((epsilonLogDerivSheafHom f θ).hom.app (op V) (Additive.ofMul s)) =
      epsilonLogDeriv θ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V) (mem_preimage f θ hz) s :=
  (congrArg (skyscraperAddSheafVal (k := k) X (squishedPoint f θ) hz)
      (epsilonLogDerivSheafHom_app f θ V (mem_comp f θ hz) s)).trans
    (skyscraperAddSheafVal_mk X (squishedPoint f θ) hz _)

/-- The `ε`-coefficient of the pullback of a section already vanishes, by the sequence of
additive sheaves. -/
private theorem epsilonCoefficientAt_pullback_eq_zero {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    {X' X : Scheme.{u}} [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ) (V : X.Opens)
    (hz : squishedPoint f θ ∈ V) (s : Γ(X, V)) :
    epsilonCoefficientAt θ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V) (mem_preimage f θ hz) ((f.app V).hom s) = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨ψ, hzeroAdd, -, hψ⟩ := shortExact_addSheaf f θ h
  have hzero : ψ.hom.app (op V) ((f.app V).hom s) = 0 :=
    congrArg (fun m => m.hom.app (op V) s) hzeroAdd
  have hev := congrArg (skyscraperAddSheafVal (k := k) X (squishedPoint f θ) hz) hzero
  rw [hψ V hz ((f.app V).hom s), skyscraperAddSheafVal_mk] at hev
  exact hev.trans (skyscraperAddSheafVal_zero X (squishedPoint f θ) hz)

/-- The two maps of the sequence of sheaves of units compose to zero: the `ε`-coefficient of the
pullback of a section already vanishes, by the sequence of additive sheaves. -/
theorem unitsPushforwardMap_comp_epsilonLogDerivSheafHom {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    {X' X : Scheme.{u}} [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ) :
    unitsPushforwardMap f ≫ epsilonLogDerivSheafHom f θ = 0 := by
  apply Sheaf.hom_ext
  ext U s
  obtain ⟨V⟩ := U
  change X.Opens at V
  obtain ⟨su, rfl⟩ : ∃ su : Γ(X, V)ˣ, Additive.ofMul su = s := ⟨s, rfl⟩
  show (epsilonLogDerivSheafHom f θ).hom.app (op V)
    ((unitsPushforwardMap f).hom.app (op V) (Additive.ofMul su)) = 0
  by_cases hz : squishedPoint f θ ∈ V
  · refine (skyscraperAddSheafVal_eq_zero_iff X (squishedPoint f θ) hz).1 ?_
    refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun t => skyscraperAddSheafVal (k := k) X (squishedPoint f θ) hz
      ((epsilonLogDerivSheafHom f θ).hom.app (op V) t))
        (unitsPushforwardMap_app f V su)) ?_
    exact (epsilonLogDerivSheafHom_val f θ V hz _).trans
      ((epsilonLogDeriv_eq_zero_iff θ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V) (mem_preimage f θ hz) _).2
        (epsilonCoefficientAt_pullback_eq_zero f θ h V hz _))
  · exact skyscraperAddSheaf_eq_zero X (squishedPoint f θ) V hz _

/-- **The short exact sequence of sheaves of units of the squishing of a tangent vector.**
If `f : X' ⟶ X` squishes the tangent vector `ϑ` of `X'` to the rational point `x` of `X`, then

`1 ⟶ 𝒪_X^* ⟶ f_*𝒪_{X'}^* ⟶ (k, +)_x ⟶ 1`

is a short exact sequence of sheaves of abelian groups on `X`, the first map being pullback of
units along `f` and the second the logarithmic `ε`-derivative along `ϑ`. Both maps are pinned
down on sections — by `Stacks.GlueSquishUnits.unitsPushforwardMap_app` and
`Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.epsilonLogDerivSheafHom_app` — so the sequence is the one of
[Stacks, Tag 0C1N] and not merely some exact sequence with those terms.

Injectivity of the first map and exactness in the middle hold already on sections over every
open. Surjectivity of the second is local at the contracted point, where it is the surjectivity
of the logarithmic `ε`-derivative on the units of the stalk of `f_*𝒪_{X'}`; away from the
contracted point the skyscraper has no sections. -/
@[stacks 0C1K "the units short exact sequence"]
theorem shortExact_units_of_isSquishingTangentVector {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k]
    {X' X : Scheme.{u}} [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ) :
    (ShortComplex.mk (unitsPushforwardMap f) (epsilonLogDerivSheafHom f θ)
      (unitsPushforwardMap_comp_epsilonLogDerivSheafHom f θ h)).ShortExact := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨ψ, hzeroAdd, hshortAdd, hψ⟩ := shortExact_addSheaf f θ h
  obtain ⟨hfOver, -, -, -, -, -, hθOver, -, -, -, -, ⟨U0, hU0, -⟩, -⟩ := id h
  have hmemU0 (y : X) : y ∈ U0 ↔ y ≠ squishedPoint f θ := by
    show y ∈ (U0 : Set X) ↔ _
    rw [hU0]
    rfl
  -- The quotient map of the additive sequence, read as a scalar.
  have hcoef (V : X.Opens) (hz : squishedPoint f θ ∈ V) (s : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ V)) :
      skyscraperAddSheafVal (k := k) X (squishedPoint f θ) hz (ψ.hom.app (op V) s) =
        epsilonCoefficientAt θ (f ⁻¹ᵁ V) (mem_preimage f θ hz) s := by
    rw [hψ V hz s, skyscraperAddSheafVal_mk]
  have hdlog := epsilonLogDerivSheafHom_val f θ
  -- Injectivity of `f.app V`, from monomorphy of the first map of the additive sequence.
  have hmonoSheaf : Mono (structureToPushforwardAddSheaf f) := hshortAdd.mono_f
  have hmonoAdd : Mono (structureToPushforwardAddSheaf f).hom :=
    Functor.map_mono (TopCat.Sheaf.forget AddCommGrpCat.{u} X)
      (structureToPushforwardAddSheaf f)
  have hinj (V : X.Opens) : Function.Injective (f.app V).hom :=
    (AddCommGrpCat.mono_iff_injective
      ((structureToPushforwardAddSheaf f).hom.app (op V))).mp inferInstance
  -- Sectionwise exactness of the additive sequence.
  have hker (V : X.Opens) (b : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ V)) (hb : ψ.hom.app (op V) b = 0) :
      ∃ a, (f.app V).hom a = b :=
    TopCat.Sheaf.sections_exact_of_left_exact
      (S := ShortComplex.mk (structureToPushforwardAddSheaf f) ψ hzeroAdd)
      hshortAdd.exact hshortAdd.mono_f b hb
  -- A unit is killed by the logarithmic derivative exactly when it is killed additively.
  have hψzero (V : X.Opens) (s : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ V)ˣ) :
      (epsilonLogDerivSheafHom f θ).hom.app (op V) (Additive.ofMul s) = 0 ↔
        ψ.hom.app (op V) (s : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ V)) = 0 := by
    by_cases hz : squishedPoint f θ ∈ V
    · refine (skyscraperAddSheafVal_eq_zero_iff X (squishedPoint f θ) hz).symm.trans
        (Iff.trans ?_ (skyscraperAddSheafVal_eq_zero_iff X (squishedPoint f θ) hz))
      rw [hdlog V hz s, epsilonLogDeriv_eq_zero_iff, hcoef V hz]
    · exact iff_of_true (skyscraperAddSheaf_eq_zero X (squishedPoint f θ) V hz _)
        (skyscraperAddSheaf_eq_zero X (squishedPoint f θ) V hz _)
  refine { exact := ?_, mono_f := ?_, epi_g := ?_ }
  · -- Exactness in the middle, already on sections.
    refine exact_of_sections _ fun V s hs => ?_
    change X.Opens at V
    obtain ⟨su, rfl⟩ : ∃ su : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ V)ˣ, Additive.ofMul su = s := ⟨s, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := units_map_range_of_values (f.app V).hom.toMonoidHom (hinj V) su
      (hker V (su : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ V)) ((hψzero V su).mp hs))
      (hker V ((su⁻¹ : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ V)ˣ) : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ V))
        ((hψzero V su⁻¹).mp (by
          show (epsilonLogDerivSheafHom f θ).hom.app (op V)
            (-(Additive.ofMul su)) = 0
          exact (((epsilonLogDerivSheafHom f θ).hom.app (op V)).hom.map_neg
            (Additive.ofMul su)).trans ((congrArg Neg.neg hs).trans neg_zero))))
    exact ⟨Additive.ofMul a, (unitsPushforwardMap_app f V a).trans
      (congrArg Additive.ofMul ha)⟩
  · -- Monomorphy of the first map.
    have hm (V : (Opens X)ᵒᵖ) : Mono ((unitsPushforwardMap f).hom.app V) := by
      obtain ⟨V⟩ := V
      change X.Opens at V
      refine (AddCommGrpCat.mono_iff_injective _).mpr fun a b hab => ?_
      have key : Units.map (f.app V).hom.toMonoidHom (a : Γ(X, V)ˣ) =
          Units.map (f.app V).hom.toMonoidHom (b : Γ(X, V)ˣ) :=
        Additive.ofMul.injective
          ((unitsPushforwardMap_app f V (a : Γ(X, V)ˣ)).symm.trans
            (hab.trans (unitsPushforwardMap_app f V (b : Γ(X, V)ˣ))))
      exact Units.ext (hinj V (congrArg Units.val key))
    exact (TopCat.Sheaf.forget AddCommGrpCat.{u} X).mono_of_mono_map
      (NatTrans.mono_of_mono_app (unitsPushforwardMap f).hom)
  · -- Surjectivity of the logarithmic derivative, local at the contracted point.
    have hlocal : TopCat.Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective ψ.hom :=
      (TopCat.Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi ψ).mpr hshortAdd.epi_g
    have hsnd (a : X.presheaf.stalk (squishedPoint f θ)) :
        (pushforwardStalkToDualNumber f θ (stalkToPushforwardStalk f θ a)).snd = 0 := by
      obtain ⟨V, hzV, s, rfl⟩ := X.presheaf.exists_germ_eq a
      exact Eq.trans (congrArg TrivSqZeroExt.snd
        ((congrArg (fun b => pushforwardStalkToDualNumber f θ b)
            (stalkToPushforwardStalk_germ f θ V hzV s)).trans
          (pushforwardStalkToDualNumber_germ f θ V hzV ((f.app V).hom s))))
        (epsilonCoefficientAt_pullback_eq_zero f θ h V hzV s)
    have hfst (a : X.presheaf.stalk (squishedPoint f θ)) :
        (pushforwardStalkToDualNumber f θ (stalkToPushforwardStalk f θ a)).fst =
          stalkToBase f θ a :=
      congrArg TrivSqZeroExt.fst
        (pushforwardStalkToDualNumber_stalkToPushforwardStalk f θ a)
    have hkerd (b : (pushforwardRingedSpace f).presheaf.stalk (squishedPoint f θ))
        (hb : pushforwardStalkCoefficient f θ b = 0) :
        ∃ a, stalkToPushforwardStalk f θ a = b := by
      obtain ⟨V, hzV, s, rfl⟩ := (pushforwardRingedSpace f).presheaf.exists_germ_eq b
      have hh : ψ.hom.app (op V) s = 0 :=
        (skyscraperAddSheafVal_eq_zero_iff X (squishedPoint f θ) hzV).1
          ((hcoef V hzV s).trans ((congrArg TrivSqZeroExt.snd
            (pushforwardStalkToDualNumber_germ f θ V hzV s)).symm.trans hb))
      obtain ⟨a, ha⟩ := hker V s hh
      exact ⟨X.presheaf.germ V (squishedPoint f θ) hzV a,
        (stalkToPushforwardStalk_germ f θ V hzV a).trans
          (congrArg (fun t => (pushforwardRingedSpace f).presheaf.germ V
            (squishedPoint f θ) hzV t) ha)⟩
    have hd : Function.Surjective (pushforwardStalkCoefficient f θ) := by
      intro c
      obtain ⟨V, hV, ⟨s, hs⟩, hzV⟩ :=
        (TopCat.Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff ψ.hom).mp hlocal ⊤
          (skyscraperAddSheafMk X (squishedPoint f θ) (Opens.mem_top _) c)
          (squishedPoint f θ) trivial
      have hs' : ψ.hom.app (op V) s =
          (skyscraperAddSheaf (k := k) X (squishedPoint f θ)).obj.map (homOfLE hV).op
            (skyscraperAddSheafMk X (squishedPoint f θ) (Opens.mem_top _) c) := hs
      refine ⟨(pushforwardRingedSpace f).presheaf.germ V (squishedPoint f θ) hzV s, ?_⟩
      refine Eq.trans (congrArg TrivSqZeroExt.snd
        (pushforwardStalkToDualNumber_germ f θ V hzV s)) ?_
      refine Eq.trans (hcoef V hzV s).symm ?_
      refine Eq.trans (congrArg
        (skyscraperAddSheafVal (k := k) X (squishedPoint f θ) hzV) hs') ?_
      refine Eq.trans (skyscraperAddSheafVal_res X (squishedPoint f θ) (homOfLE hV) hzV _) ?_
      exact skyscraperAddSheafVal_mk X (squishedPoint f θ) (Opens.mem_top _) c
    have hrange : Function.Surjective (stalkToBase f θ) := by
      refine constantCoefficient_surjective (θ ≫ f) ?_
      rw [Category.assoc, hfOver.comp_over, hθOver]
    have hfinite : (stalkToPushforwardStalk f θ).Finite :=
      finite_of_coefficient_sequence (stalkToPushforwardStalk f θ)
        (pushforwardStalkToDualNumber f θ) (stalkToBase f θ)
        (pushforwardStalkCoefficient f θ) hfst hsnd
        (pushforwardStalkCoefficient_eq f θ) hkerd hd hrange
    have hsurj := dlog_units_surjective_of_coefficient_sequence
      (stalkToPushforwardStalk f θ) (pushforwardStalkToDualNumber f θ) (stalkToBase f θ)
      (pushforwardStalkCoefficient f θ) hfst hsnd (pushforwardStalkCoefficient_eq f θ)
      hkerd hd hrange (fun a ha => map_maximalIdeal_le_jacobson_of_integral
        (stalkToPushforwardStalk f θ) hfinite.to_isIntegral
        (Ideal.mem_map_of_mem (stalkToPushforwardStalk f θ) ha))
    refine (TopCat.Sheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff_epi (epsilonLogDerivSheafHom f θ)).mp ?_
    rw [TopCat.Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_iff]
    intro V t y hy
    by_cases hyz : y = squishedPoint f θ
    · subst hyz
      obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := hsurj (skyscraperAddSheafVal (k := k) X (squishedPoint f θ) hy t)
      obtain ⟨W, hWV, hzW, s, hs⟩ :=
        exists_unit_germ (pushforwardRingedSpace f) (squishedPoint f θ) b hy
      refine ⟨W, hWV, ⟨Additive.ofMul s, ?_⟩, hzW⟩
      refine skyscraperAddSheafVal_injective X (squishedPoint f θ) hzW ?_
      refine Eq.trans (hdlog W hzW s) ?_
      refine Eq.trans ?_
        (skyscraperAddSheafVal_res X (squishedPoint f θ) (homOfLE hWV) hzW t).symm
      refine Eq.trans ?_ hb
      refine Eq.trans (dualNumberDlogHom_germ f θ W hzW s).symm ?_
      exact congrArg (fun c => dualNumberDlogHom
        (Additive.ofMul (Units.map (pushforwardStalkToDualNumber f θ).toMonoidHom c))) hs
    · refine ⟨V ⊓ U0, inf_le_left, ⟨0, ?_⟩, ⟨hy, (hmemU0 y).2 hyz⟩⟩
      refine Eq.trans (map_zero _) ?_
      refine (skyscraperAddSheaf_eq_zero X (squishedPoint f θ) (V ⊓ U0) ?_ _).symm
      exact fun hzz => ((hmemU0 _).1 hzz.2) rfl

/-! ### The tangent homomorphism to the Picard group -/

open Stacks.Cohomology.AbelianColimit (abSections H'functor H'δ)

open Stacks.GluePicard (h0Iso h1UnitsAddEquivOfScheme)

/-- The short complex of sheaves of units of a squishing, at the spelling of the site of opens,
which is the spelling the long exact cohomology sequence works in. -/
def unitsComplex {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] (f : X' ⟶ X)
    (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ) :
    ShortComplex (Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) AddCommGrpCat.{u}) :=
  ShortComplex.mk (unitsPushforwardMap f) (epsilonLogDerivSheafHom f θ)
    (unitsPushforwardMap_comp_epsilonLogDerivSheafHom f θ h)

/-- That short complex is short exact. -/
theorem unitsComplex_shortExact {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] (f : X' ⟶ X)
    (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ) :
    (unitsComplex f θ h).ShortExact :=
  shortExact_units_of_isSquishingTangentVector f θ h

/-- The sections of the quotient sheaf of the units sequence over the whole space are the ground
field. The source is spelled through the sections functor, which is the spelling the long exact
sequence works in. -/
def sequenceTopIso {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] (f : X' ⟶ X)
    (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ) :
    (abSections (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤).obj (unitsComplex f θ h).X₃ ≅ AddCommGrpCat.of k :=
  eqToIso (skyscraperAddSheaf_obj_eq X (squishedPoint f θ) (Opens.mem_top _))

/-- **The quotient map of the units sequence on sections over the whole space is the logarithmic
`ε`-derivative**, in the spelling of the sections functor. -/
theorem sequenceTopIso_map_g {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] (f : X' ⟶ X)
    (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ)
    (t : (abSections (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤).obj (unitsComplex f θ h).X₂) :
    (sequenceTopIso f θ h).hom
        ((abSections (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤).map (unitsComplex f θ h).g t) =
      epsilonLogDeriv θ (f ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : X.Opens))
        (mem_preimage f θ (Opens.mem_top _))
        (Additive.toMul (α := Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : X.Opens))ˣ) t) :=
  epsilonLogDerivSheafHom_val f θ ⊤ (Opens.mem_top _)
    (Additive.toMul (α := Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : X.Opens))ˣ) t)

/-- The connecting map of the units sequence, read on `(k, +)` through the sections of the
additive skyscraper over the whole space and on cohomology through the identification of
degree-zero native cohomology with sections. -/
def connectingHom {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] (f : X' ⟶ X)
    (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ) :
    AddCommGrpCat.of k ⟶
      (H'functor (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤ 1).obj (unitsSheaf X.toRingedSpace) :=
  (sequenceTopIso f θ h).inv ≫ (h0Iso (X : Type u)).inv.app (unitsComplex f θ h).X₃ ≫
    H'δ (unitsComplex_shortExact f θ h) ⊤ (zero_add 1)

/-- The connecting map, on a scalar. -/
theorem connectingHom_apply {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] (f : X' ⟶ X)
    (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ) (c : k) :
    AddCommGrpCat.Hom.hom' (connectingHom f θ h) c =
      H'δ (unitsComplex_shortExact f θ h) (⊤ : Opens (X : Type u)) (zero_add 1)
        ((h0Iso (X : Type u)).inv.app (unitsComplex f θ h).X₃
          ((sequenceTopIso f θ h).inv c)) :=
  rfl

/-- **The tangent homomorphism `(k, +) ⟶ Pic(X)` of [Stacks, Tag 0C1N].** It is the connecting
homomorphism of the short exact sequence of sheaves of units of a squishing, read through the
five-term low-degree cohomology sequence over the whole space and through the identification of
`H¹(X, 𝒪_X^*)` with the Picard group of [Stacks, Tag 09NU]. -/
@[stacks 0C1N "the tangent homomorphism"]
def picardTangentHom {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] (f : X' ⟶ X)
    (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ) : k →+ Stacks.Picard.ofScheme X where
  toFun c := h1UnitsAddEquivOfScheme X (AddCommGrpCat.Hom.hom' (connectingHom f θ h) c)
  map_zero' := by rw [map_zero, map_zero]
  map_add' c d := by rw [map_add, map_add]

/-- The tangent homomorphism is the connecting map followed by the identification of first
cohomology with the Picard group. -/
theorem picardTangentHom_apply {k : Type u} [Field k] [IsAlgClosed k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}}
    [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))] (f : X' ⟶ X)
    (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ) (c : k) :
    picardTangentHom f θ h c =
      h1UnitsAddEquivOfScheme X (AddCommGrpCat.Hom.hom' (connectingHom f θ h) c) :=
  rfl

/-- **Exactness of the five-term low-degree sequence at `(k, +)`**: a scalar killed by the
connecting map of the units sequence is the logarithmic `ε`-derivative of a unit on the whole
of `X'`. -/
theorem exists_unit_epsilonLogDeriv_eq_of_connectingHom_eq_zero {k : Type u} [Field k]
    [IsAlgClosed k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}} [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ) (c : k)
    (h0 : AddCommGrpCat.Hom.hom' (connectingHom f θ h) c = 0) :
    ∃ s : Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : X.Opens))ˣ,
      epsilonLogDeriv θ (f ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : X.Opens)) (mem_preimage f θ (Opens.mem_top _)) s = c := by
  classical
  rw [connectingHom_apply] at h0
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ := (ShortComplex.ab_exact_iff _).1
    (Stacks.Cohomology.AbelianColimit.shortComplex_H'_exact₃
      (unitsComplex_shortExact f θ h) (⊤ : Opens (X : Type u)) (zero_add 1)) _ h0
  have hy' : (H'functor (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤ 0).map (unitsComplex f θ h).g y =
      (h0Iso (X : Type u)).inv.app (unitsComplex f θ h).X₃
        ((sequenceTopIso f θ h).inv c) := hy
  have hnat : (h0Iso (X : Type u)).hom.app (unitsComplex f θ h).X₃
        ((H'functor (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤ 0).map (unitsComplex f θ h).g y) =
      (abSections (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤).map (unitsComplex f θ h).g
        ((h0Iso (X : Type u)).hom.app (unitsComplex f θ h).X₂ y) := by
    have hn := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom
      ((h0Iso (X : Type u)).hom.naturality (unitsComplex f θ h).g) y
    rwa [ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ConcreteCategory.comp_apply] at hn
  have hval : (abSections (X := (X : Type u)) ⊤).map (unitsComplex f θ h).g
        ((h0Iso (X : Type u)).hom.app (unitsComplex f θ h).X₂ y) =
      (sequenceTopIso f θ h).inv c := by
    rw [← hnat, hy']
    simp
  have hkey := sequenceTopIso_map_g f θ h
    ((h0Iso (X : Type u)).hom.app (unitsComplex f θ h).X₂ y)
  rw [hval] at hkey
  refine ⟨Additive.toMul (α := Γ(X', f ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : X.Opens))ˣ)
    ((h0Iso (X : Type u)).hom.app (unitsComplex f θ h).X₂ y), ?_⟩
  rw [← hkey]
  simp

/-- **A scalar killed by the tangent homomorphism is the logarithmic `ε`-derivative of a unit on
the whole of `X'`**; equivalently, the kernel of the tangent homomorphism is the image of
`𝒪^*(X') → (k, +)`. -/
theorem exists_globalUnit_epsilonLogDeriv_eq_of_picardTangentHom_eq_zero {k : Type u} [Field k]
    [IsAlgClosed k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}} [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ) (c : k)
    (hc : picardTangentHom f θ h c = 0) :
    ∃ s : Γ(X', ⊤)ˣ, epsilonLogDeriv θ ⊤ (Opens.mem_top _) s = c := by
  refine exists_unit_epsilonLogDeriv_eq_of_connectingHom_eq_zero f θ h c ?_
  refine (h1UnitsAddEquivOfScheme X).injective ?_
  rw [← picardTangentHom_apply, hc, map_zero]

/-- **The tangent homomorphism is injective when `X'` is proper and reduced.** A scalar in its
kernel is the logarithmic `ε`-derivative of a unit on `X'`, and on a proper reduced `X'` the
logarithmic `ε`-derivative of a global unit vanishes by
`Stacks.SquishSheafSequence.epsilonLogDeriv_eq_zero_of_isProper_of_isReduced`. -/
@[stacks 0C1N "injectivity on a proper reduced scheme"]
theorem injective_picardTangentHom_of_isProper_of_isReduced {k : Type u} [Field k]
    [IsAlgClosed k] {X' X : Scheme.{u}} [X'.Over (Spec (.of k))] [X.Over (Spec (.of k))]
    (f : X' ⟶ X) (θ : Spec (.of (DualNumber k)) ⟶ X')
    (h : AlgebraicGeometry.IsSquishingTangentVector f θ)
    [IsProper (X' ↘ Spec (.of k))] [IsReduced X'] :
    Function.Injective (picardTangentHom f θ h) := by
  intro c d hcd
  have hzero : picardTangentHom f θ h (c - d) = 0 := by rw [map_sub, hcd, sub_self]
  obtain ⟨s, hs⟩ :=
    exists_globalUnit_epsilonLogDeriv_eq_of_picardTangentHom_eq_zero f θ h (c - d) hzero
  rw [epsilonLogDeriv_eq_zero_of_isProper_of_isReduced f θ h s] at hs
  exact sub_eq_zero.mp hs.symm

end Stacks.SquishSheafSequence

end
